  }]], "2ColumnTableMod",ExpressionUUID->"6c213eb1-1323-401c-adab-\
e1ef8b645374"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For the flows of two vector fields at scale ",
 StyleBox["r", "TI"],
 " the loop moves each point by ",
 StyleBox["r\.b2", "TI"],
 " times the Lie bracket ",
 StyleBox["[X, Y]", "TI"],
 ", up to ",
 StyleBox["O(r\.b3)", "TI"],
 " and the sign convention of the bracket, so a loop that closes reads a \
vanishing bracket. On a graph the loop is a displacement, multivalued where \
an inverse or a negative is."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"4753ee2e-09e1-4a05-aa6c-da2694eb3299"],

Cell["\<\
The commutator of two automorphisms is an automorphism, and exchanging the \
two displacements inverts it.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"0b1d8b85-7cf0-42b1-ab9b-f88f215bb4ca"]
}, Open  ]],

